<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar buys 10,000T U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar buys 10,000T U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp on Wednesday bought 10,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow corn from Cargill, traders said.  </p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis at 92 U.S. cents per tonne over March Chicago futures, traders said.</p>
<p>The shipment was slated for delivery from February 5-25 from the U.S. Gulf of Mexico or February 26 to March 10 from the Pacific Northwest, they said.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
